        try {
            engine.eval(code);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

3) Root Cause
The root cause is the direct inclusion of untrusted user input into the evaluated code without any form of validation, sanitization, or neutralization. This allows attackers to craft input that, when evaluated, executes arbitrary malicious code.

