1) Vulnerability Description:
The code fails to properly invalidate or clean up cache entries when an exception occurs during data fetching. Specifically, when an exception is thrown, the cache may contain stale or inconsistent data, leading to potential data integrity issues. This is an example of CWE-460: Improper Cleanup on Thrown Exception, where resources (in this case, cache entries) are not adequately handled after an error.

