The root cause is performing subtraction that exceeds the safe margin near the minimum integer limit (`Integer.MIN_VALUE`). When `value` is close to `Integer.MIN_VALUE`, subtracting a larger number causes the result to wrap around, resulting in an incorrect value due to underflow.

