1) Vulnerability Description
The code exhibits an Integer Underflow vulnerability related to array index calculation. Specifically, subtracting 1 from the minimum integer value (`Integer.MIN_VALUE`) causes an underflow, resulting in an invalid array index that can lead to runtime exceptions or unexpected behavior.

2) Vulnerable Code
```java
public class VulnerableExample7 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = {1, 2, 3};
        int index = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int result = array[index - 1]; // Underflow in index calculation leads to exception
        System.out.println("Array value: " + result);
    }
}
```

