1. Vulnerability Description:
The code relies on package-private (default) access modifiers to store and provide access to database credentials. This approach exposes sensitive information (username and password) within the package scope, increasing the risk of unintended access or modification. Such reliance on package-level visibility constitutes CWE-487: Reliance on Package-level Scope, which can lead to security vulnerabilities if other classes within the same package are compromised or malicious.

