1) **Vulnerability Description:**

The provided Java WebSocket client code establishes a WebSocket connection over an unencrypted channel. As a result, any data transmitted—including sensitive information such as Social Security Numbers (SSNs)—is sent in plaintext. This exposes the data to potential interception and eavesdropping by malicious actors, leading to confidentiality breaches.

