### 3) Root Cause
The root cause of this vulnerability is the use of the `HTTP` protocol instead of `HTTPS` for transmitting sensitive data. HTTP transmits data in plaintext, making it susceptible to interception, eavesdropping, and man-in-the-middle attacks. The code lacks encryption or secure communication protocols, leading to potential compromise of sensitive information.

