        scheduler.schedule(() -> {
            throw new RuntimeException("Unexpected error"); // exception not caught
        }, 1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
    }
}
```

3. Root Cause
The root cause is the absence of exception handling within the scheduled task. The lambda expression directly throws a RuntimeException without wrapping it in a try-catch block. In Java, uncaught exceptions in a thread cause that thread to terminate, and in the case of scheduled tasks, it can prevent further execution or proper thread management.

