            System.out.println(obj);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("JSON parsing failed: " + e.getMessage());
            // Additional handling or fallback logic here
        }
    }
}
```

---

**Summary**: Proper exception handling around JSON parsing prevents unhandled exceptions, enhances application stability, and reduces security risks associated with application crashes or information leakage.

