3) Root Cause
The core issue is the reliance on catching a NullPointerException to handle a null `content`. When `content` is null, calling `content.toString()` results in an NPE. Instead of proactively checking if `content` is null, the code allows the exception to occur and then handles it via catch block, which is an anti-pattern and can lead to less maintainable code.

