The root cause of this vulnerability is the direct invocation of socket operations within an EJB method. Sockets may introduce security vulnerabilities, hinder scalability, and create potential attack vectors if not properly managed. Additionally, establishing network connections from enterprise beans violates best practices, as it couples business logic directly with network I/O, which is better handled through dedicated services or layers.

