- Stability Issues: Improper management of socket resources might lead to resource leaks and application instability.
- Scalability Concerns: Opening sockets directly in EJBs can hinder transaction management and clustering capabilities.
- Compliance Violations: May violate organizational policies regarding network security and best practices.

5. Mitigation
- Avoid performing network I/O within EJBs; delegate such operations to dedicated service components or external adapters.
- Use higher-level APIs or messaging systems (e.g., JMS, REST APIs) to transfer data instead of raw sockets.
